P7. Signedness against the congruence argument
==============================================

F = 0 throughout, so this isolates signedness from the fraction axis
that P2b and P2c already established. Exhaustive over the whole
signed domain at each width, both operand orders, every triple.

--- signed W = 3, domain [-4, 3], overflow = wrap ---
    (a+b)+c == a+(b+c)     HOLDS  (0/512)
    (a*b)*c == a*(b*c)     HOLDS  (0/512)
    a*(b+c) == a*b+a*c     HOLDS  (0/512)
--- signed W = 3, domain [-4, 3], overflow = saturate ---
    (a+b)+c == a+(b+c)     FAILS  108/512 = 21.09%   first: a=-4,b=-4,c=1 -> -3 vs -4
    (a*b)*c == a*(b*c)     FAILS  28/512 =  5.47%   first: a=-4,b=-4,c=-1 -> -3 vs -4
    a*(b+c) == a*b+a*c     FAILS  120/512 = 23.44%   first: a=-4,b=-4,c=1 -> 3 vs -1
--- signed W = 4, domain [-8, 7], overflow = wrap ---
    (a+b)+c == a+(b+c)     HOLDS  (0/4096)
    (a*b)*c == a*(b*c)     HOLDS  (0/4096)
    a*(b+c) == a*b+a*c     HOLDS  (0/4096)
--- signed W = 4, domain [-8, 7], overflow = saturate ---
    (a+b)+c == a+(b+c)     FAILS  952/4096 = 23.24%   first: a=-8,b=-8,c=1 -> -7 vs -8
    (a*b)*c == a*(b*c)     FAILS  160/4096 =  3.91%   first: a=-8,b=-8,c=-1 -> -7 vs -8
    a*(b+c) == a*b+a*c     FAILS  1414/4096 = 34.52%   first: a=-8,b=-8,c=1 -> 7 vs -1
--- signed W = 5, domain [-16, 15], overflow = wrap ---
    (a+b)+c == a+(b+c)     HOLDS  (0/32768)
    (a*b)*c == a*(b*c)     HOLDS  (0/32768)
    a*(b+c) == a*b+a*c     HOLDS  (0/32768)
--- signed W = 5, domain [-16, 15], overflow = saturate ---
    (a+b)+c == a+(b+c)     FAILS  7920/32768 = 24.17%   first: a=-16,b=-16,c=1 -> -15 vs -16
    (a*b)*c == a*(b*c)     FAILS  780/32768 =  2.38%   first: a=-16,b=-16,c=-1 -> -15 vs -16
    a*(b+c) == a*b+a*c     FAILS  13594/32768 = 41.49%   first: a=-16,b=-16,c=1 -> 15 vs -1
--- signed W = 6, domain [-32, 31], overflow = wrap ---
    (a+b)+c == a+(b+c)     HOLDS  (0/262144)
    (a*b)*c == a*(b*c)     HOLDS  (0/262144)
    a*(b+c) == a*b+a*c     HOLDS  (0/262144)
--- signed W = 6, domain [-32, 31], overflow = saturate ---
    (a+b)+c == a+(b+c)     FAILS  64480/262144 = 24.60%   first: a=-32,b=-32,c=1 -> -31 vs -32
    (a*b)*c == a*(b*c)     FAILS  3516/262144 =  1.34%   first: a=-32,b=-32,c=-1 -> -31 vs -32
    a*(b+c) == a*b+a*c     FAILS  119422/262144 = 45.56%   first: a=-32,b=-32,c=1 -> 31 vs -1
--- signed W = 7, domain [-64, 63], overflow = wrap ---
    (a+b)+c == a+(b+c)     HOLDS  (0/2097152)
    (a*b)*c == a*(b*c)     HOLDS  (0/2097152)
    a*(b+c) == a*b+a*c     HOLDS  (0/2097152)
--- signed W = 7, domain [-64, 63], overflow = saturate ---
    (a+b)+c == a+(b+c)     FAILS  520128/2097152 = 24.80%   first: a=-64,b=-64,c=1 -> -63 vs -64
    (a*b)*c == a*(b*c)     FAILS  15036/2097152 =  0.72%   first: a=-64,b=-64,c=-1 -> -63 vs -64
    a*(b+c) == a*b+a*c     FAILS  1000674/2097152 = 47.72%   first: a=-64,b=-64,c=1 -> 63 vs -1

Reading:

The prediction holds and phase one's F1a is narrower than it read.
Signed WRAPPING is a ring at every swept width, so all three laws
hold, exactly as in the unsigned case: reduction mod 2^W is still a
congruence when the representatives are re-centred.

Signed SATURATION is not, and the mechanism is the two-sided clamp.
A one-sided clamp is a congruence because nothing below the bound
can be pushed back across it by a monotone operation. With a clamp
at each end, multiplication by a negative value carries a value
across from one bound to the other, and the collapse stops
respecting the operation.

So the signedness dimension is not free on this axis, and any
finding of the form 'the laws hold at F = 0' has to carry its
signedness. Phase one's F1 and F1a both listed `signedness =
unsigned`, which the notation says means they hold nowhere else.
That was the right reading and this is why.
